# Design Patterns Blog Posts

Reference implementation: `content/design-patterns/single-responsibility-principle.md`, `content/design-patterns/strategy-pattern.md`

## Repo Layout

| Path | Purpose |
|---|---|
| `content/design-patterns/_index.md` | Section landing page |
| `content/design-patterns/<topic>.md` | One post per principle, pattern, or case study |
| `data/design_patterns_modules.yaml` | Module grouping and topic order |
| `data/design_patterns_order.yaml` | Flat topic order (derived from modules) |
| `layouts/shortcodes/impl-tabs.html` | Tab container shortcode |
| `layouts/shortcodes/impl-tab.html` | Per-language panel shortcode |
| `layouts/partials/impl-tabs-head.html` | Tab bar + panel CSS (site-wide) |
| `layouts/partials/extend_footer.html` | Tab switch JS (`activateImplTab`, click delegation) |

URL pattern: `/design-patterns/<filename>/`

## Hugo Front Matter

```yaml
---
title: "<Topic Title>"
date: 2026-06-30T10:00:00+00:00
draft: true
description: "One-line summary for SEO and social previews."
tags: ["lld", "<topic-tag>", "java", "golang", "python"]
categories: ["Design Patterns"]
shortTitle: "<Short Title>"
module: 1
moduleTitle: "SOLID & Design Foundations"
sectionRef: "1.1"
languages: ["java", "golang", "python"]
---
```

Set `draft: false` when the post is ready to publish.

## Required Sections (use `###` headings)

Microservices-style posts use `###` so section collapsibles group content cleanly.

1. **Problem & Intent** — what design problem this solves (2–3 sentences)
2. **When to Use / When NOT to Use** — decision table (always include anti-use cases)
3. **Structure (Class Diagram)** — Mermaid `classDiagram`
4. **Interaction Flow** — Mermaid `sequenceDiagram` or `flowchart TD`
5. **Implementation** — **all code snippets** inside Java / Go / Python `impl-tabs` (see below)
6. **Trade-offs & Operational Realities** — table of complexity, testability, framework fit
7. **Junior Mistakes** — common misapplications
8. **Senior Questions** — numbered interview probes
9. **Revision Cheat Sheet** — 30-second recall bullets
10. **See Also** — links to related LLD topics and cross-curriculum posts

Separate major sections with `---` horizontal rules.

---

## Code Snippets — Mandatory `impl-tabs` Rule

**Every code snippet in an LLD post that shows implementation belongs inside `impl-tabs`.** Do not render Java and Go as separate vertical sections or as adjacent fenced blocks outside the shortcode.

### When to use `impl-tabs`

| Content type | Use `impl-tabs`? | Notes |
|---|---|---|
| Java / Go / Python implementation code | **Yes — required** | Under `### Implementation` |
| Anti-pattern vs fixed example (multiple blocks) | **Yes** | Put all Java blocks in `lang="java"` tab; all Go blocks in `lang="golang"` tab; Python in `lang="python"` tab |
| Mermaid diagrams | **No** | Keep in Structure / Interaction Flow sections |
| One-line inline `` `code` `` in prose | **No** | Fine in any section |
| Shell / YAML / config-only examples | **No** | Rare in LLD; if needed, single tab or prose only |

### When NOT to use (forbidden patterns)

| Do NOT | Why |
|---|---|
| `### Implementation (Java)` + `### Implementation (Go)` | Stacks languages vertically; breaks revision layout |
| Raw ` ```java` / ` ```go` blocks directly under `### Implementation` | Bypasses tabs; page grows vertically |
| `{< impl-tabs >}` (single brace) | Hugo will not parse shortcodes — use `{{< >}}` |
| `impl-tab` without matching `java="..."` / `golang="..."` on parent | Tab bar renders empty |
| `lang="go"` on `impl-tab` | Must be `lang="golang"` to match `data-tab` on buttons |

### Canonical template

```markdown
### Implementation

{{< impl-tabs default="java" java="Java" golang="Go" python="Python" >}}
{{< impl-tab lang="java" >}}

**Violation — describe the smell:**

```java
// bad example
```

**Fixed — describe the approach:**

```java
// good example
```

{{< /impl-tab >}}
{{< impl-tab lang="golang" >}}

**Violation:**

```go
// bad example
```

**Fixed:**

```go
// good example
```

{{< /impl-tab >}}
{{< impl-tab lang="python" >}}

**Violation:**

```python
# bad example
```

**Fixed:**

```python
# good example
```

{{< /impl-tab >}}
{{< /impl-tabs >}}
```

### Shortcode contract

| Shortcode | Required params | Notes |
|---|---|---|
| `impl-tabs` | `default="java"`, `java="Java"`, `golang="Go"`, `python="Python"` | Tab labels on parent; `default` controls initial visible panel |
| `impl-tab` | `lang="java"`, `lang="golang"`, or `lang="python"` | Must match a key passed to `impl-tabs` |

- Use `{{<` / `>}}` delimiters (not `{{% %}}`) when panels contain fenced code blocks.
- **Java tab first** (default); **Go second**; **Python third**.
- If Go or Python port is not ready yet, keep a minimal stub in that tab — do not omit the tab.
- Active panel max-height `28rem` with internal scroll — long code scrolls inside the tab, not down the page.

### Language conventions

| Language | Convention |
|----------|------------|
| **Java** | Interfaces for abstractions; Spring mentions in architecture posts only when relevant |
| **Go** | Small interfaces; composition over inheritance; no forced "pattern ceremony" |
| **Python** | `typing.Protocol`, dataclasses, functions as strategies; favor explicit composition over inheritance |

